basalt-nonfree: the Basalt OS repository for non-free drivers

Off by default. It holds drivers that are not free software but may be
redistributed, packaged by OpenBasalt for Basalt OS:

- the NVIDIA driver for GPUs of the Turing generation and newer
  (nvidia-driver, nvidia-driver-compute for servers): NVIDIA's open GPU
  kernel modules, built and signed for every Basalt OS kernel, and
  NVIDIA's userspace, unmodified, under the NVIDIA Driver License
  Agreement.

Install it from Settings, Additional drivers, or with the assistant:
basalt drivers. Both show the license and what changes before anything
is installed, take a snapshot first, and check the driver after the next
start. Details: https://github.com/basalt-os/basalt-os/blob/main/docs/nvidia.md

Source code: the source RPMs are in the same repository
(basalt-nonfree-source, https://obpkg.org/basalt-nonfree/<release>/source/).

Packaged by OpenBasalt, not supported by NVIDIA. NVIDIA, GeForce and CUDA
are trademarks of NVIDIA Corporation.
